// Title: XBAP Execution From Uncommon Locations Via PresentationHost.EXE
// Sigma ID: d22e2925-cfd8-463f-96f6-89cec9d9bc5f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-01 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects the execution of ".xbap" (Browser Applications) files via PresentationHost.EXE from an
//   uncommon location. These files can be abused to run malicious ".xbap" files any bypass AWL
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate ".xbap" being executed via "PresentationHost"
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Presentationhost/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_presentationhost_uncommon_location_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\presentationhost.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "PresentationHost.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains ".xbap") and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains " C:\\Windows\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains " C:\\Program Files")))
